# OpenLogo code ownership — GitHub requests a listed owner's review on matching paths, and
# (when the branch's protection/ruleset has "Require review from Code Owners" enabled) BLOCKS
# merge until that owner approves. CODEOWNERS assigns the required *reviewer*; it does not by
# itself restrict who clicks merge — the branch ruleset does. This is the teeth behind the
# "maintainer-only, non-delegable" rule for spec/ and the saga/spec governance surfaces, and it
# only holds while the rulesets on `main` and `saga/*` require code-owner review (see
# devops/branching-and-commits/SKILL.md → "Required branch protection"). See also
# .github/skills/shared/definition-of-done.md (merge authority).

# Everything in the spec is maintainer-owned language/architecture governance ([spec]).
/spec/                                  @pmalarme

# The saga and spec issue templates define the maintainer-only governance surfaces.
/.github/ISSUE_TEMPLATE/saga.yml        @pmalarme
/.github/ISSUE_TEMPLATE/spec.yml        @pmalarme

# Governance config itself (ownership + merge convention) stays maintainer-owned.
/.github/CODEOWNERS                     @pmalarme
